Windows can report nested virtualization support for WHPX and still refuse
to enable it (hr=80370302). QEMU then stopped the VM, so Cage turned the
in-hypervisor local APIC off for every host, which made guest timers and
inter-processor interrupts slow. Continue without nested virtualization.

--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -3198,10 +3198,14 @@
             WHvPartitionPropertyCodeNestedVirtualization,
             &prop,
             sizeof(WHV_PARTITION_PROPERTY));
-            if (FAILED(hr)) {
-                error_report("WHPX: Failed to enable nested virtualization, hr=%08lx", hr);
-                ret = -EINVAL;
-                goto error;
+        /*
+         * Windows can report nested virtualization support and still refuse
+         * to enable it (hr=80370302). A guest that runs no hypervisor of its
+         * own needs neither: keep the in-hypervisor local APIC and continue.
+         */
+        if (FAILED(hr)) {
+            warn_report("WHPX: Failed to enable nested virtualization, hr=%08lx; "
+                        "continuing without it", hr);
         }
     }
 
